operation getTitlePointerAt
input getTitlePointerAt titlesBuffer COpaqueMemoryAddress
input getTitlePointerAt todoIndex CSignedInt64
input getTitlePointerAt titleCapacity CSignedInt64
output getTitlePointerAt COpaqueMemoryAddress
memoryHeap getTitlePointerAt no
async getTitlePointerAt no
purpose getTitlePointerAt "Return the start pointer for one title slot in the contiguous title array."
invariant getTitlePointerAt "The returned pointer is titlesBuffer plus todoIndex multiplied by titleCapacity."
invariant getTitlePointerAt "This operation is the *title-stride* half of the implicit `TodoEntry` record. The corresponding done flag for the same todoIndex lives at byte offset todoIndex in the sibling doneArray (stride 1). A future refactor that introduces `record TodoEntry { field done Bool, field title CNullTerminatedByteString }` plus `recordLayout TodoEntry column` would replace this pointer arithmetic with declarative field access; until that exists, every reader/writer of the two arrays must obey the same-index rule documented in `invariant main` (todo data shape)."
label startGetTitlePointerAt
call offsetCall math.multiplyI64
arg offsetCall left todoIndex
arg offsetCall right titleCapacity
run offsetCall
bind titleOffset CSignedInt64 offsetCall
call pointerCall pointer.offset
arg pointerCall base titlesBuffer
arg pointerCall offset titleOffset
run pointerCall
bind titlePointer COpaqueMemoryAddress pointerCall
returnValue titlePointer

operation writeEmptyBuffer
input writeEmptyBuffer targetBuffer COpaqueMemoryAddress
output writeEmptyBuffer CSignedInt64
effect writeEmptyBuffer write memory.buffer
authority writeEmptyBuffer memory.buffer write
memoryHeap writeEmptyBuffer no
async writeEmptyBuffer no
purpose writeEmptyBuffer "Store a leading NUL so a title-edit buffer starts empty."
invariant writeEmptyBuffer "After success targetBuffer contains an empty C string."
label startWriteEmptyBuffer
storage local immutable zeroOffset CSignedInt64 0
call storeNulCall pointer.storeByte
arg storeNulCall buffer targetBuffer
arg storeNulCall offset zeroOffset
arg storeNulCall value nulByte
run storeNulCall
returnValue zeroOffset

operation copyStringBuffer
input copyStringBuffer sourceBuffer COpaqueMemoryAddress
input copyStringBuffer targetBuffer COpaqueMemoryAddress
input copyStringBuffer targetBufferCapacity CSignedInt64
output copyStringBuffer CSignedInt64
effect copyStringBuffer read memory.buffer
effect copyStringBuffer write memory.buffer
authority copyStringBuffer memory.buffer read
authority copyStringBuffer memory.buffer write
memoryHeap copyStringBuffer no
async copyStringBuffer no
purpose copyStringBuffer "Copy a bounded null-terminated title string into another buffer."
invariant copyStringBuffer "The target buffer is always null-terminated and the returned value is its copied length."
label startCopyStringBuffer
storage local immutable zeroIndex CSignedInt64 0
storage local immutable oneStep CSignedInt64 1
storage local mutable readIndex CSignedInt64 zeroIndex
storage local mutable writeIndex CSignedInt64 zeroIndex
call maxWritableIndexCall math.subtractI64
arg maxWritableIndexCall left targetBufferCapacity
arg maxWritableIndexCall right oneStep
run maxWritableIndexCall
bind maxWritableIndex CSignedInt64 maxWritableIndexCall
label copyStringBufferLoop
call loadSourceByteCall pointer.loadByte
arg loadSourceByteCall buffer sourceBuffer
arg loadSourceByteCall offset readIndex
run loadSourceByteCall
bind sourceByte CSignedInt32 loadSourceByteCall
call nulCheckCall math.equalCSignedInt32
arg nulCheckCall left sourceByte
arg nulCheckCall right nulByte
run nulCheckCall
bind sourceByteIsNul Bool nulCheckCall
branchIf sourceByteIsNul finishCopyStringBuffer
call capacityCheckCall math.greaterThanOrEqualI64
arg capacityCheckCall left writeIndex
arg capacityCheckCall right maxWritableIndex
run capacityCheckCall
bind targetBufferFull Bool capacityCheckCall
branchIf targetBufferFull finishCopyStringBuffer
call storeTargetByteCall pointer.storeByte
arg storeTargetByteCall buffer targetBuffer
arg storeTargetByteCall offset writeIndex
arg storeTargetByteCall value sourceByte
run storeTargetByteCall
call incrementReadIndexCall math.addI64
arg incrementReadIndexCall left readIndex
arg incrementReadIndexCall right oneStep
run incrementReadIndexCall
bind nextReadIndex CSignedInt64 incrementReadIndexCall
set local readIndex nextReadIndex
call incrementWriteIndexCall math.addI64
arg incrementWriteIndexCall left writeIndex
arg incrementWriteIndexCall right oneStep
run incrementWriteIndexCall
bind nextWriteIndex CSignedInt64 incrementWriteIndexCall
set local writeIndex nextWriteIndex
branch copyStringBufferLoop
label finishCopyStringBuffer
call terminateTargetCall pointer.storeByte
arg terminateTargetCall buffer targetBuffer
arg terminateTargetCall offset writeIndex
arg terminateTargetCall value nulByte
run terminateTargetCall
returnValue writeIndex

operation appendPrintableKeyToBuffer
input appendPrintableKeyToBuffer targetBuffer COpaqueMemoryAddress
input appendPrintableKeyToBuffer currentLength CSignedInt64
input appendPrintableKeyToBuffer bufferCapacity CSignedInt64
input appendPrintableKeyToBuffer keyCode TuiKeyCode
output appendPrintableKeyToBuffer CSignedInt64
effect appendPrintableKeyToBuffer write memory.buffer
authority appendPrintableKeyToBuffer memory.buffer write
memoryHeap appendPrintableKeyToBuffer no
async appendPrintableKeyToBuffer no
purpose appendPrintableKeyToBuffer "Append one printable key to the edit buffer when there is room."
invariant appendPrintableKeyToBuffer "The target buffer remains null-terminated and currentLength never grows past capacity minus one."
warning appendPrintableKeyToBuffer "Only single-byte printable ASCII input (codepoints 32..126) is accepted. Multi-byte UTF-8 input, terminal paste blocks, control characters, and IME composition sequences are silently dropped here; supporting them requires a UTF-8 decoder and a separate paste-mode reader, neither of which exists yet."
label startAppendPrintableKeyToBuffer
storage local immutable oneStep CSignedInt64 1
# rationale: The inclusive ASCII printable range. 32 = ' ' (space, the lowest
# printable character) and 126 = '~' (tilde, the highest before DEL at 127).
# Bytes outside [32..126] are dropped — see the warning on this operation.
storage local immutable minPrintableKey CSignedInt32 32
storage local immutable maxPrintableKey CSignedInt32 126
call belowPrintableCheckCall math.lessThanCSignedInt32
arg belowPrintableCheckCall left keyCode
arg belowPrintableCheckCall right minPrintableKey
run belowPrintableCheckCall
bind belowPrintable Bool belowPrintableCheckCall
branchIf belowPrintable skipAppendPrintableKey
call abovePrintableCheckCall math.greaterThanCSignedInt32
arg abovePrintableCheckCall left keyCode
arg abovePrintableCheckCall right maxPrintableKey
run abovePrintableCheckCall
bind abovePrintable Bool abovePrintableCheckCall
branchIf abovePrintable skipAppendPrintableKey
call maxWritableIndexCall math.subtractI64
arg maxWritableIndexCall left bufferCapacity
arg maxWritableIndexCall right oneStep
run maxWritableIndexCall
bind maxWritableIndex CSignedInt64 maxWritableIndexCall
call capacityCheckCall math.greaterThanOrEqualI64
arg capacityCheckCall left currentLength
arg capacityCheckCall right maxWritableIndex
run capacityCheckCall
bind bufferFull Bool capacityCheckCall
branchIf bufferFull skipAppendPrintableKey
call storeKeyCall pointer.storeByte
arg storeKeyCall buffer targetBuffer
arg storeKeyCall offset currentLength
arg storeKeyCall value keyCode
run storeKeyCall
call incrementLengthCall math.addI64
arg incrementLengthCall left currentLength
arg incrementLengthCall right oneStep
run incrementLengthCall
bind nextLength CSignedInt64 incrementLengthCall
call terminateBufferCall pointer.storeByte
arg terminateBufferCall buffer targetBuffer
arg terminateBufferCall offset nextLength
arg terminateBufferCall value nulByte
run terminateBufferCall
returnValue nextLength
label skipAppendPrintableKey
returnValue currentLength

operation deleteLastBufferByte
input deleteLastBufferByte targetBuffer COpaqueMemoryAddress
input deleteLastBufferByte currentLength CSignedInt64
output deleteLastBufferByte CSignedInt64
effect deleteLastBufferByte write memory.buffer
authority deleteLastBufferByte memory.buffer write
memoryHeap deleteLastBufferByte no
async deleteLastBufferByte no
purpose deleteLastBufferByte "Remove the last edit-buffer byte for backspace handling."
invariant deleteLastBufferByte "The target buffer remains null-terminated and length never goes below zero."
label startDeleteLastBufferByte
storage local immutable zeroLength CSignedInt64 0
storage local immutable oneStep CSignedInt64 1
call emptyCheckCall math.equalI64
arg emptyCheckCall left currentLength
arg emptyCheckCall right zeroLength
run emptyCheckCall
bind bufferIsEmpty Bool emptyCheckCall
branchIf bufferIsEmpty skipDeleteLastBufferByte
call decrementLengthCall math.subtractI64
arg decrementLengthCall left currentLength
arg decrementLengthCall right oneStep
run decrementLengthCall
bind nextLength CSignedInt64 decrementLengthCall
call terminateBufferCall pointer.storeByte
arg terminateBufferCall buffer targetBuffer
arg terminateBufferCall offset nextLength
arg terminateBufferCall value nulByte
run terminateBufferCall
returnValue nextLength
label skipDeleteLastBufferByte
returnValue currentLength

operation copyFixedTodoJsonTitleAtOffset
input copyFixedTodoJsonTitleAtOffset sourceLine COpaqueMemoryAddress
input copyFixedTodoJsonTitleAtOffset titleBuffer COpaqueMemoryAddress
input copyFixedTodoJsonTitleAtOffset valueOffset CSignedInt64
input copyFixedTodoJsonTitleAtOffset titleBufferCapacity CSignedInt64
output copyFixedTodoJsonTitleAtOffset CSignedInt64
effect copyFixedTodoJsonTitleAtOffset read memory.buffer
effect copyFixedTodoJsonTitleAtOffset write memory.buffer
authority copyFixedTodoJsonTitleAtOffset memory.buffer read
authority copyFixedTodoJsonTitleAtOffset memory.buffer write
memoryHeap copyFixedTodoJsonTitleAtOffset no
async copyFixedTodoJsonTitleAtOffset no
purpose copyFixedTodoJsonTitleAtOffset "Copy a fixed todo JSON title value into a caller-owned C string buffer."
invariant copyFixedTodoJsonTitleAtOffset "Only the exact object shape emitted by saveTodosToJson is supported; only quote and backslash escapes emitted by saveTodosToJson are decoded."
label startCopyFixedTodoJsonTitleAtOffset
storage local immutable zeroIndex CSignedInt64 0
storage local immutable oneStep CSignedInt64 1
# rationale: readIndex is seeded directly from valueOffset so the loop starts
# at the first character after `"title":"`. The earlier zeroIndex initializer
# was dead because `set local readIndex valueOffset` immediately overwrote it.
storage local mutable readIndex CSignedInt64 valueOffset
storage local mutable writeIndex CSignedInt64 zeroIndex
call maxWritableIndexCall math.subtractI64
arg maxWritableIndexCall left titleBufferCapacity
arg maxWritableIndexCall right oneStep
run maxWritableIndexCall
bind maxWritableIndex CSignedInt64 maxWritableIndexCall
label copyTitleLoop
call loadTitleByteCall pointer.loadByte
arg loadTitleByteCall buffer sourceLine
arg loadTitleByteCall offset readIndex
run loadTitleByteCall
bind titleByte CSignedInt32 loadTitleByteCall
call quoteCheckCall math.equalCSignedInt32
arg quoteCheckCall left titleByte
arg quoteCheckCall right quoteByte
run quoteCheckCall
bind titleByteIsQuote Bool quoteCheckCall
branchIf titleByteIsQuote finishCopyTitle
call newlineCheckCall math.equalCSignedInt32
arg newlineCheckCall left titleByte
arg newlineCheckCall right newlineByte
run newlineCheckCall
bind titleByteIsNewline Bool newlineCheckCall
branchIf titleByteIsNewline finishCopyTitle
call carriageReturnCheckCall math.equalCSignedInt32
arg carriageReturnCheckCall left titleByte
arg carriageReturnCheckCall right carriageReturnByte
run carriageReturnCheckCall
bind titleByteIsCarriageReturn Bool carriageReturnCheckCall
branchIf titleByteIsCarriageReturn finishCopyTitle
call nulCheckCall math.equalCSignedInt32
arg nulCheckCall left titleByte
arg nulCheckCall right nulByte
run nulCheckCall
bind titleByteIsNul Bool nulCheckCall
branchIf titleByteIsNul finishCopyTitle
call backslashCheckCall math.equalCSignedInt32
arg backslashCheckCall left titleByte
arg backslashCheckCall right backslashByte
run backslashCheckCall
bind titleByteIsBackslash Bool backslashCheckCall
branchIf titleByteIsBackslash copyEscapedTitleByte
call capacityCheckCall math.greaterThanOrEqualI64
arg capacityCheckCall left writeIndex
arg capacityCheckCall right maxWritableIndex
run capacityCheckCall
bind titleBufferFull Bool capacityCheckCall
branchIf titleBufferFull finishCopyTitle
call storeTitleByteCall pointer.storeByte
arg storeTitleByteCall buffer titleBuffer
arg storeTitleByteCall offset writeIndex
arg storeTitleByteCall value titleByte
run storeTitleByteCall
call incrementReadIndexCall math.addI64
arg incrementReadIndexCall left readIndex
arg incrementReadIndexCall right oneStep
run incrementReadIndexCall
bind nextReadIndex CSignedInt64 incrementReadIndexCall
set local readIndex nextReadIndex
call incrementWriteIndexCall math.addI64
arg incrementWriteIndexCall left writeIndex
arg incrementWriteIndexCall right oneStep
run incrementWriteIndexCall
bind nextWriteIndex CSignedInt64 incrementWriteIndexCall
set local writeIndex nextWriteIndex
branch copyTitleLoop
label copyEscapedTitleByte
call escapedReadIndexCall math.addI64
arg escapedReadIndexCall left readIndex
arg escapedReadIndexCall right oneStep
run escapedReadIndexCall
bind escapedReadIndex CSignedInt64 escapedReadIndexCall
call loadEscapedByteCall pointer.loadByte
arg loadEscapedByteCall buffer sourceLine
arg loadEscapedByteCall offset escapedReadIndex
run loadEscapedByteCall
bind escapedTitleByte CSignedInt32 loadEscapedByteCall
call escapedNewlineCheckCall math.equalCSignedInt32
arg escapedNewlineCheckCall left escapedTitleByte
arg escapedNewlineCheckCall right newlineByte
run escapedNewlineCheckCall
bind escapedByteIsNewline Bool escapedNewlineCheckCall
branchIf escapedByteIsNewline finishCopyTitle
call escapedCarriageReturnCheckCall math.equalCSignedInt32
arg escapedCarriageReturnCheckCall left escapedTitleByte
arg escapedCarriageReturnCheckCall right carriageReturnByte
run escapedCarriageReturnCheckCall
bind escapedByteIsCarriageReturn Bool escapedCarriageReturnCheckCall
branchIf escapedByteIsCarriageReturn finishCopyTitle
call escapedNulCheckCall math.equalCSignedInt32
arg escapedNulCheckCall left escapedTitleByte
arg escapedNulCheckCall right nulByte
run escapedNulCheckCall
bind escapedByteIsNul Bool escapedNulCheckCall
branchIf escapedByteIsNul finishCopyTitle
call escapedCapacityCheckCall math.greaterThanOrEqualI64
arg escapedCapacityCheckCall left writeIndex
arg escapedCapacityCheckCall right maxWritableIndex
run escapedCapacityCheckCall
bind escapedTitleBufferFull Bool escapedCapacityCheckCall
branchIf escapedTitleBufferFull finishCopyTitle
call storeEscapedTitleByteCall pointer.storeByte
arg storeEscapedTitleByteCall buffer titleBuffer
arg storeEscapedTitleByteCall offset writeIndex
arg storeEscapedTitleByteCall value escapedTitleByte
run storeEscapedTitleByteCall
call advancePastEscapedByteCall math.addI64
arg advancePastEscapedByteCall left escapedReadIndex
arg advancePastEscapedByteCall right oneStep
run advancePastEscapedByteCall
bind nextEscapedReadIndex CSignedInt64 advancePastEscapedByteCall
set local readIndex nextEscapedReadIndex
call incrementEscapedWriteIndexCall math.addI64
arg incrementEscapedWriteIndexCall left writeIndex
arg incrementEscapedWriteIndexCall right oneStep
run incrementEscapedWriteIndexCall
bind nextEscapedWriteIndex CSignedInt64 incrementEscapedWriteIndexCall
set local writeIndex nextEscapedWriteIndex
branch copyTitleLoop
label finishCopyTitle
call terminateTitleCall pointer.storeByte
arg terminateTitleCall buffer titleBuffer
arg terminateTitleCall offset writeIndex
arg terminateTitleCall value nulByte
run terminateTitleCall
returnValue writeIndex

operation parseJsonFlagAtOffset
input parseJsonFlagAtOffset sourceLine COpaqueMemoryAddress
input parseJsonFlagAtOffset valueOffset CSignedInt64
output parseJsonFlagAtOffset CSignedInt32
effect parseJsonFlagAtOffset read memory.buffer
authority parseJsonFlagAtOffset memory.buffer read
memoryHeap parseJsonFlagAtOffset no
async parseJsonFlagAtOffset no
purpose parseJsonFlagAtOffset "Parse a zero-or-one flag from a fixed todo JSON field offset."
invariant parseJsonFlagAtOffset "Only ASCII one maps to one; every other byte maps to zero."
label startParseJsonFlagAtOffset
storage local immutable zeroFlag CSignedInt32 0
storage local immutable oneFlag CSignedInt32 1
call loadFlagByteCall pointer.loadByte
arg loadFlagByteCall buffer sourceLine
arg loadFlagByteCall offset valueOffset
run loadFlagByteCall
bind flagByte CSignedInt32 loadFlagByteCall
call flagOneCheckCall math.equalCSignedInt32
arg flagOneCheckCall left flagByte
arg flagOneCheckCall right oneAsciiByte
run flagOneCheckCall
bind flagIsOne Bool flagOneCheckCall
branchIf flagIsOne parsedOneFlag
returnValue zeroFlag
label parsedOneFlag
returnValue oneFlag

operation renderTodoRow
input renderTodoRow doneArray COpaqueMemoryAddress
input renderTodoRow titlesBuffer COpaqueMemoryAddress
input renderTodoRow actualIndex CSignedInt64
input renderTodoRow selectedIndex CSignedInt64
input renderTodoRow todoCount CSignedInt64
input renderTodoRow titleCapacity CSignedInt64
output renderTodoRow CSignedInt32
effect renderTodoRow read memory.buffer
effect renderTodoRow write console.stdout
authority renderTodoRow memory.buffer read
authority renderTodoRow console.stdout write
memoryHeap renderTodoRow no
async renderTodoRow no
purpose renderTodoRow "Render one visible table row from the heap-backed todo arrays."
invariant renderTodoRow "Rendering reads todo arrays but does not mutate todo state."
invariant renderTodoRow "todoRowFormatText's `%3lld` index column reserves three digits, which assumes todoCapacity <= 999. If todoCapacity grows past 999, the column will widen and the table borders in topFrameText/bottomFrameText/blankRowText will misalign. Update all four format constants in lockstep when bumping todoCapacity."
warning renderTodoRow "todoRowFormatText's `%-40.40s` title column silently truncates titles longer than 40 bytes to 40 bytes on screen. The underlying titlesArray slot is still titleCapacity bytes (currently 128); only the rendered display is clipped. Editing a truncated row in the modal shows the full underlying title, not the truncated form."
label startRenderTodoRow
storage local immutable oneValue CSignedInt64 1
storage local immutable doneFlagValue CSignedInt32 1
storage local immutable normalMarkerText CNullTerminatedByteString " "
storage local immutable selectedMarkerText CNullTerminatedByteString ">"
storage local immutable openStatusText CNullTerminatedByteString "[ ]"
storage local immutable doneStatusText CNullTerminatedByteString "[x]"
storage local immutable addRowText CNullTerminatedByteString "(new note)"
storage local immutable blankRowText CNullTerminatedByteString "  |       |      |                                          |\n"
storage local immutable todoRowFormatText CNullTerminatedByteString "  | %s %3lld | %s  | %-40.40s |\n"
storage local immutable addRowFormatText CNullTerminatedByteString "  | %s   + |      | %-40.40s |\n"
storage local mutable markerText CNullTerminatedByteString normalMarkerText
storage local mutable statusText CNullTerminatedByteString openStatusText
call selectedCheckCall math.equalI64
arg selectedCheckCall left actualIndex
arg selectedCheckCall right selectedIndex
run selectedCheckCall
bind rowIsSelected Bool selectedCheckCall
branchIf rowIsSelected markSelectedRow
branch chooseRowKind
label markSelectedRow
set local markerText selectedMarkerText
branch chooseRowKind
label chooseRowKind
call existingRowCheckCall math.lessThanI64
arg existingRowCheckCall left actualIndex
arg existingRowCheckCall right todoCount
run existingRowCheckCall
bind rowIsExistingTodo Bool existingRowCheckCall
branchIf rowIsExistingTodo renderExistingTodoRow
call addRowCheckCall math.equalI64
arg addRowCheckCall left actualIndex
arg addRowCheckCall right todoCount
run addRowCheckCall
bind rowIsAddTodo Bool addRowCheckCall
branchIf rowIsAddTodo renderAddTodoRow
call blankRowCall c.printf
arg blankRowCall format blankRowText
run blankRowCall
ignoreValue blankRowCall CSignedInt32
returnValue successCode
label renderAddTodoRow
call addRowCall c.printf
arg addRowCall format addRowFormatText
arg addRowCall marker markerText
arg addRowCall title addRowText
run addRowCall
ignoreValue addRowCall CSignedInt32
returnValue successCode
label renderExistingTodoRow
call doneLoadCall pointer.loadByte
arg doneLoadCall buffer doneArray
arg doneLoadCall offset actualIndex
run doneLoadCall
bind doneValue CSignedInt32 doneLoadCall
call doneCheckCall math.equalCSignedInt32
arg doneCheckCall left doneValue
arg doneCheckCall right doneFlagValue
run doneCheckCall
bind rowIsDone Bool doneCheckCall
branchIf rowIsDone markDoneRow
branch renderExistingTodoLine
label markDoneRow
set local statusText doneStatusText
branch renderExistingTodoLine
label renderExistingTodoLine
call titlePointerCall getTitlePointerAt
arg titlePointerCall titlesBuffer titlesBuffer
arg titlePointerCall todoIndex actualIndex
arg titlePointerCall titleCapacity titleCapacity
run titlePointerCall
bind titlePointer COpaqueMemoryAddress titlePointerCall
call displayNumberCall math.addI64
arg displayNumberCall left actualIndex
arg displayNumberCall right oneValue
run displayNumberCall
bind displayNumber CSignedInt64 displayNumberCall
call rowCall c.printf
arg rowCall format todoRowFormatText
arg rowCall marker markerText
arg rowCall number displayNumber
arg rowCall status statusText
arg rowCall title titlePointer
run rowCall
ignoreValue rowCall CSignedInt32
returnValue successCode

operation renderScreen
input renderScreen doneArray COpaqueMemoryAddress
input renderScreen titlesBuffer COpaqueMemoryAddress
input renderScreen todoCount CSignedInt64
input renderScreen selectedIndex CSignedInt64
input renderScreen topIndex CSignedInt64
input renderScreen screenMode ScreenMode
input renderScreen editBuffer COpaqueMemoryAddress
input renderScreen editLength CSignedInt64
input renderScreen titleCapacity CSignedInt64
input renderScreen visibleRows CSignedInt64
input renderScreen statusText CNullTerminatedByteString
output renderScreen CSignedInt32
effect renderScreen read memory.buffer
effect renderScreen write console.stdout
authority renderScreen memory.buffer read
authority renderScreen console.stdout write
memoryHeap renderScreen no
async renderScreen no
purpose renderScreen "Render the todo TUI from heap-backed arrays with a fixed-width edit modal."
invariant renderScreen "The visible row loop emits at most visibleRows rows and does not mutate todo state."
invariant renderScreen "editBuffer is an opaque memory pointer that callers guarantee holds a null-terminated byte sequence: writeEmptyBuffer seeds the first byte with NUL on allocation, and appendPrintableKeyToBuffer / deleteLastBufferByte maintain the terminator at every length change. renderScreen passes editBuffer to c.printf as a %s argument, which relies on that invariant."
warning renderScreen "modalValueFormatText's `%-47.47s` edit-modal title column silently truncates titles longer than 47 bytes on screen. The full editBuffer (up to titleCapacity-1 = 127 bytes) is still in memory; only the modal view is clipped. The character-count line below (modalMetaFormatText) shows the true length so an editor of a long title knows the visible region is partial."
label startRenderScreen
storage local immutable zeroValue CSignedInt64 0
storage local immutable oneValue CSignedInt64 1
storage local immutable topFrameText CNullTerminatedByteString "  TODO TUI                                              todos.json\n  +-------+------+------------------------------------------+\n  | Sel   | Done | Note                                     |\n  +-------+------+------------------------------------------+"
storage local immutable bottomFrameText CNullTerminatedByteString "  +-------+------+------------------------------------------+"
storage local immutable statusFormatText CNullTerminatedByteString "\n  Status: %s\n"
storage local immutable navigationText CNullTerminatedByteString "  Up/Down select | Right edit/new | Enter/Space done | D delete | Esc quit"
storage local immutable modalTopText CNullTerminatedByteString "\n  +----------------------------------------------------+\n  | Edit note                                          |"
storage local immutable modalValueFormatText CNullTerminatedByteString "  | > %-47.47s |\n"
storage local immutable modalMetaFormatText CNullTerminatedByteString "  |   characters: %-3lld                                |\n"
storage local immutable modalHelpText CNullTerminatedByteString "  | Enter save | Esc cancel | Backspace delete         |\n  +----------------------------------------------------+"
storage local mutable visibleRowCursor CSignedInt64 zeroValue
call clearCall clearScreen
run clearCall
ignoreValue clearCall CSignedInt32
call topCall c.puts
arg topCall text topFrameText
run topCall
ignoreValue topCall CSignedInt32
label renderRowsLoop
call rowsDoneCheckCall math.greaterThanOrEqualI64
arg rowsDoneCheckCall left visibleRowCursor
arg rowsDoneCheckCall right visibleRows
run rowsDoneCheckCall
bind rowsDone Bool rowsDoneCheckCall
branchIf rowsDone finishRows
call actualIndexCall math.addI64
arg actualIndexCall left topIndex
arg actualIndexCall right visibleRowCursor
run actualIndexCall
bind actualIndex CSignedInt64 actualIndexCall
call renderRowCall renderTodoRow
arg renderRowCall doneArray doneArray
arg renderRowCall titlesBuffer titlesBuffer
arg renderRowCall actualIndex actualIndex
arg renderRowCall selectedIndex selectedIndex
arg renderRowCall todoCount todoCount
arg renderRowCall titleCapacity titleCapacity
run renderRowCall
ignoreValue renderRowCall CSignedInt32
call advanceVisibleRowCall math.addI64
arg advanceVisibleRowCall left visibleRowCursor
arg advanceVisibleRowCall right oneValue
run advanceVisibleRowCall
bind nextVisibleRowCursor CSignedInt64 advanceVisibleRowCall
set local visibleRowCursor nextVisibleRowCursor
branch renderRowsLoop
label finishRows
call bottomCall c.puts
arg bottomCall text bottomFrameText
run bottomCall
ignoreValue bottomCall CSignedInt32
call statusCall c.printf
arg statusCall format statusFormatText
arg statusCall status statusText
run statusCall
ignoreValue statusCall CSignedInt32
call editModeCheckCall ScreenMode.equal
arg editModeCheckCall left screenMode
arg editModeCheckCall right EditMode
run editModeCheckCall
bind isEditMode Bool editModeCheckCall
branchIf isEditMode renderModal
call navigationCall c.puts
arg navigationCall text navigationText
run navigationCall
ignoreValue navigationCall CSignedInt32
returnValue successCode
label renderModal
call modalTopCall c.puts
arg modalTopCall text modalTopText
run modalTopCall
ignoreValue modalTopCall CSignedInt32
call modalValueCall c.printf
arg modalValueCall format modalValueFormatText
arg modalValueCall title editBuffer
run modalValueCall
ignoreValue modalValueCall CSignedInt32
call modalMetaCall c.printf
arg modalMetaCall format modalMetaFormatText
arg modalMetaCall length editLength
run modalMetaCall
ignoreValue modalMetaCall CSignedInt32
call modalHelpCall c.puts
arg modalHelpCall text modalHelpText
run modalHelpCall
ignoreValue modalHelpCall CSignedInt32
returnValue successCode

operation clampTopIndex
input clampTopIndex selectedIndex CSignedInt64
input clampTopIndex topIndex CSignedInt64
input clampTopIndex visibleRows CSignedInt64
output clampTopIndex CSignedInt64
memoryHeap clampTopIndex no
async clampTopIndex no
purpose clampTopIndex "Keep the selected row inside the visible scroll window."
label startClampTopIndex
storage local immutable oneValue CSignedInt64 1
call selectedBeforeTopCall math.lessThanI64
arg selectedBeforeTopCall left selectedIndex
arg selectedBeforeTopCall right topIndex
run selectedBeforeTopCall
bind selectedBeforeTop Bool selectedBeforeTopCall
branchIf selectedBeforeTop returnSelectedAsTop
call visibleLimitCall math.addI64
arg visibleLimitCall left topIndex
arg visibleLimitCall right visibleRows
run visibleLimitCall
bind visibleLimit CSignedInt64 visibleLimitCall
call selectedPastVisibleCall math.greaterThanOrEqualI64
arg selectedPastVisibleCall left selectedIndex
arg selectedPastVisibleCall right visibleLimit
run selectedPastVisibleCall
bind selectedPastVisible Bool selectedPastVisibleCall
branchIf selectedPastVisible computeScrolledTop
returnValue topIndex
label returnSelectedAsTop
returnValue selectedIndex
label computeScrolledTop
call subtractRowsCall math.subtractI64
arg subtractRowsCall left selectedIndex
arg subtractRowsCall right visibleRows
run subtractRowsCall
bind selectedMinusVisibleRows CSignedInt64 subtractRowsCall
call addOneCall math.addI64
arg addOneCall left selectedMinusVisibleRows
arg addOneCall right oneValue
run addOneCall
bind scrolledTop CSignedInt64 addOneCall
returnValue scrolledTop

operation computeMaxSelectable
input computeMaxSelectable todoCount CSignedInt64
input computeMaxSelectable todoCapacity CSignedInt64
output computeMaxSelectable CSignedInt64
memoryHeap computeMaxSelectable no
async computeMaxSelectable no
purpose computeMaxSelectable "Return the last selectable row, including the new-note row when capacity remains."
invariant computeMaxSelectable "Requires todoCapacity greater than zero; zero capacity falls back to zero only as a defensive sentinel."
label startComputeMaxSelectable
storage local immutable oneValue CSignedInt64 1
storage local immutable zeroValue CSignedInt64 0
call hasAddRowCall math.lessThanI64
arg hasAddRowCall left todoCount
arg hasAddRowCall right todoCapacity
run hasAddRowCall
bind hasAddRow Bool hasAddRowCall
branchIf hasAddRow returnCountAsMax
call emptyCapacityCheckCall math.equalI64
arg emptyCapacityCheckCall left todoCapacity
arg emptyCapacityCheckCall right zeroValue
run emptyCapacityCheckCall
bind capacityIsZero Bool emptyCapacityCheckCall
branchIf capacityIsZero returnZeroMax
call lastExistingCall math.subtractI64
arg lastExistingCall left todoCount
arg lastExistingCall right oneValue
run lastExistingCall
bind lastExistingIndex CSignedInt64 lastExistingCall
returnValue lastExistingIndex
label returnCountAsMax
returnValue todoCount
label returnZeroMax
returnValue zeroValue

operation isNegativeStatus
input isNegativeStatus statusCode CSignedInt32
output isNegativeStatus Bool
